WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.270
Human hearing stops at about 20 kilohertz.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:05.890
Any sound above that is ultrasound.

3
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.040
Medical scanners go much higher
still: about 1 to 15 megahertz.

4
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:13.410
Nobody in the room hears a thing.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.450
Yet a picture of a baby
builds up on the screen.

6
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.090
How can sound that nobody
hears draw that picture?

7
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.400
In this mission, you'll find out what
limits how fine the detail in a scan can

8
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.210
be.

9
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.450
Then you'll read a scan
taken along a single line,

10
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.070
and measure a layer deep inside.

11
00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.230
Your mission: explain how a sound nobody
can hear can draw a picture of a baby

12
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.640
before it is born.
